  "raw": {
    "https://follett.com/who-we-help/faculty/": {
      "title": "You choose the course materials. We’ll ensureseamless access for students.",
      "description": "Faculty - Follett Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us Who We Help Faculty We make it simple to choose and adopt course materials, and offer solutions that ensure students have convenient, affordable access to required resources so you can start teaching effectively on the first day of class. You choose the course materials. We’ll ensure seamless access for students. Affordable Access Improves Student Outcomes Students in Access programs are more likely to persist and complete their courses. Campus-wide Access programs ensure all students get all required materials on day one. These programs have been shown to improve course completion rates by 15.5%, with even higher rates among historically underrepresented student populations. These programs don’t limit your academic freedom; instructors still have the flexibility to explore and choose the best fit materials. Learn More About Affordable Access The New, Streamlined Adoption Experience is Here! As part of our commitment to supporting every step of the academic journey, we’ve reimagined our course material adoption tool to better serve faculty and department admins. Designed in partnership with campus users, this enhanced experience prioritizes transparency of course material details and a seamless readopt process. Watch a short video to see how the improved adoption tool simplifies and enhances your workflow! Watch the Teaser We’ll Handle the Tech, So You Can Focus on Teaching Through our industry-leading academic integration tools, we’re making learning simpler and more convenient for students, faculty, and staff. With a centralized hub for information and materials, students have what they need, when they need it. This efficiency allows faculty to spend more time teaching and less time troubleshooting. See our Seamless Integrations in Action Recommended Resources VIEW ALL Podcast Improving the Course Material Adoption Experience: Reflections of a Research Roadtrip September 16, 2024 Listen to podcast Webinar How Colleges and Universities are Transforming Course Material Access and Affordability June 22, 2023 View webinar Blog Supporting Faculty Adoptions: A User-Driven Approach June 06, 2024 READ ARTICLE Watch Now Video Access Programs: The Faculty Perspective Angie Springer at Danville Area Community College shares her thoughts on the impact of Access programs, which have… Learn More Ready to see how Follett supports student success? Download the Guide Need more information? CONTACT FOLLETT CAMPUS SOLUTIONS Campus Store Course Materials Access Programs Apparel & Merchandise Fan Shops Virtual & Hybrid Stores Technology ABOUT US Our Mission The Academic Journey Meet Our Team Press & Media Careers Brand Partnerships Policies CUSTOMER SUPPORT Customer Support Center Contact Us Find Your Campus Store RESOURCES Podcasts & Videos Campus Connections Blog Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook Terms of Use Privacy Policy Cookies Copyright © 2026 Follett Corporation | 3 Westbrook Corporate Center, Westchester, IL 60154"
    },
    "https://follett.com/about-us/careers/": {
      "title": "Join theFollettteam",
      "description": "Careers - Follett Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us About Us About Us Careers We’re looking for people who are passionate about shaping the future of higher education. Find your fit in our full-time, part-time, and seasonal roles across retail, corporate, or warehouse settings in the US or Canada. Join the Follett team We are currently hiring for several full-time, part-time, and seasonal positions. Please click below for retail, corporate, and warehouse jobs in the US or Canada. Retail Jobs Connect directly with the campuses you love. Many of our retail team members are students or alumni from the campuses they serve, fostering a unique and personal link to the academic community. Opportunities range from temporary team members to team leads and store management. View Openings Corporate Jobs Join our corporate team to play a direct role in shaping the future of higher education. We’re pioneering new approaches, practices, and solutions that help campuses thrive. Be part of an organization that is dedicated to inspiring, enabling, and celebrating the academic journey. Opportunities extend across our headquarters and other office locations. View Openings Seasonal Jobs We’re on the lookout for seasonal team members to join our dynamic crew supporting campus stores, warehouses, and events. We offer weekly pay and flexible hours with opportunities in the US and Canada. Our partner NXTThing RPO helps coordinate seasonal hiring; we’re always looking for people to join the Follett team! View Openings Follett Corporation is an Equal Opportunity Employer Reasonable Accommodation We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment, without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status, or other characteristics protected by law. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Follett is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to job applicants with disabilities. If you are interested in applying for employment and need assistance or an accommodation in the application process due to a disability, please contact us by email or phone. Email: Send request to follettaccomodations@follett.com Phone: Request assistance by calling 1.844.324.4748 (HR4U) For Hearing Impaired: Dial 7-1-1 or click on the accessibility icon We are here to answer your questions and provide assistance Monday to Friday, 7am-6pm Central Time, except national holidays. When contacting us, please provide your contact information, the job position or title, and state the nature of your accessibility issue. Notice on Recruiting Scams Thank you for your interest in Follett. We encourage you to explore job opportunities at Follett on our website, follett.com/careers . We caution you to be wary of internet, email and telephone scams in which fraudsters may try to take advantage of job seekers by pretending to represent Follett. We have been made aware of individuals and organizations falsely pretending to recruit on behalf of, or be affiliated with, Follett. Intended victims have been invited to participate in bogus interviews, asked to fill out fabricated employment applications and have even been issued fake offer letters, all with the ultimate goal of trying to entice victims to divulge sensitive personal information. These communications are fraudulent and do not originate from Follett nor are they associated with our recruitment process. We never ask job applicants for money. Follett will not send you a check (for immediate mobile deposit) to purchase equipment at any point in the recruitment process. Please note all seasonal hiring is done through our partner NXTThing RPO. To learn more about NXTTHING, visit: https://www.nxtthingrpo.com/ . How to Identify Recruiting Scams? Here are few things to watch for: Correspondence from the fraudsters are usually from free email accounts, like Yahoo!, Hotmail or Gmail. A Follett team member will not solicit candidates through a non-Follett email address or phone number. In addition, Follett does not utilize video chat rooms (e.g. Google Hangouts) to conduct interviews or contact potential candidates about a job opportunity via text messaging or instant messaging; The use of the English language, in written communication, is poor; Communications that are unsolicited or unexpected or are from an individual or website with which you are unfamiliar or whose domain name is inconsistent with that used by the actual business; Job opportunities and offers that appear “too good to be true”; Communications at the application phase requesting your social security number, national insurance number, date of birth, bank account information or other sensitive personal information; Insisting on urgency and that they are very interested in hiring you now; and, Requesting that you cash a check to purchase office equipment, or send money to Follett to purchase equipment. Follett has no responsibility for fraudulent job offers and advises interested applicants to follow the guidance provided above. If you believe you have been a victim of a recruiting scam, please: Contact your local law enforcement authorities and file a police report and provide them with all information you may have (email addresses, phone/fax details, etc., copies of emails/letters). Contact U.S. Department of Justice at www.stopfraud.gov Please email us at recruitingfraud@follett.com , and use the term “fraudulent job offer” in the subject/re box. Follett is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. © 2023 FOLLETT CORPORATION Learn more about Follett’s mission, services, and goals. Connect with us Need more information? CONTACT FOLLETT CAMPUS SOLUTIONS Campus Store Course Materials Access Programs Apparel & Merchandise Fan Shops Virtual & Hybrid Stores Technology ABOUT US Our Mission The Academic Journey Meet Our Team Press & Media Careers Brand Partnerships Policies CUSTOMER SUPPORT Customer Support Center Contact Us Find Your Campus Store RESOURCES Podcasts & Videos Campus Connections Blog Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook Terms of Use Privacy Policy Cookies Copyright © 2026 Follett Corporation | 3 Westbrook Corporate Center, Westchester, IL 60154"
    },
